# Security headers for the static SPA.
#
# Applied by Workers Static Assets at the edge. They cannot be set from worker.js:
# `run_worker_first: ["/api/*"]` in wrangler.jsonc means asset requests never reach
# Worker code, which is the point — one Worker invocation per image would be waste.
#
# The API sets its own headers via helmet; these cover the app itself, which is the
# surface that renders and prompts for wallet signatures.
#
# frame-ancestors is the one that matters here: without it any page can iframe the
# app and get a transaction approved out of context.
#
# No script-src or connect-src. The app loads wallet SDKs that open WebSockets to
# several relays and fetch remote token metadata; that policy has to be derived from
# the real list and tested against a live wallet connection, not guessed at.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
